  "comments": "Pork-knockers are freelance Guyanese prospectors who mine for diamonds and gold in the alluvial plains of the Guyanese interior. Pork-knockers have been responsible for discovering large deposits of gold and diamonds. The name &quot;pork-knockers&quot; refers to their regular diet of pickled pork of wild pig that is often eaten at the end of the day. The coin depicts a porknocker engaged in traditional small-scale gold mining.<br /><br /><br />\r\nCoins 2011 and 2013 are different because the word &quot;GUYANA&quot; is smaller on 2011 coins compared to 2013 coins.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5804e4496aa81.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5804e4496aa81.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"199\" height=\"120\" /></a>",
